From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:32:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] drm/msm/a6xx: mask the GMU-to-host interrupts before
 the GMU boots

GMU2HOST_INTR_MASK resets to 0 when the GMU power domain goes off, and
a6xx_gmu_resume() programs it only after a6xx_hfi_start(). Until then
every HFI reply during the boot raises the HFI interrupt line. The line
is disabled at that point, but lazily, so a resume nearly always
delivers it once and the flow handler masks it. When the target CPU
sits in an idle state that is slow to leave, the delivery can arrive
after enable_irq(hfi_irq), and a6xx_hfi_irq() then runs while
a6xx_gmu_set_initial_freq() and the GPU_SET OOB request poll their own
bits in the same status register.

Mask all GMU-to-host interrupts before the GMU boots. The write after
a6xx_hfi_start() still unmasks the ones we handle (the CM3 fault, and
the HFI message bit when msm.gmu_hfi_irq_fix is on).

Re-implemented from the idea of armada-os PR 662 (SuperTurtleDev
iceland-mainline-kernel-linux e04a83af3cce, posted without a
Signed-off-by); no code was copied.

Based-on: SuperTurtleDev iceland-mainline-kernel-linux e04a83af3cce (idea only; armada-os PR 662)
Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/pull/662
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index fcb567ec9..b85734e5a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1485,6 +1485,14 @@ int a6xx_gmu_resume(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu)
 	/* Set the bus quota to a reasonable value for boot */
 	a6xx_gmu_set_initial_bw(gpu, gmu);
 
+	/*
+	 * GMU2HOST_INTR_MASK reads 0 again after the GMU power domain was off.
+	 * Mask it before the GMU boots, so that HFI replies during the boot do
+	 * not raise the (lazily disabled) HFI interrupt; it is unmasked after
+	 * a6xx_hfi_start() below.
+	 */
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_MASK, ~0);
+
 	/* Enable the GMU interrupt */
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_CLR, ~0);
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_MASK, ~A6XX_GMU_IRQ_MASK);
